  "response_text": "We get the new value for PSP_val by subtracting our assumed size of main stack size and threads stack size (0x400 bytes) from the MSP_init_val. This works because stacks grow from higher memory address from lower ones, meaning the top of the stack, which is MSP, is at a higher memory address and subtracting it allows us to obtain the correct PSP_val. MSP defines the address of the start of the whole stack region. Without MSP it becomes impossible to know where the useable RAM for stacks begins.\\n",
